[node name="Documentation" type="CanvasLayer" parent="." unique_id=1970060297]
visible = false

[node name="Documentation_label" type="Label" parent="Documentation" unique_id=1918540772]
offset_right = 40.0
offset_bottom = 23.0
text = "Science Olympiad Game Agent
B-70 Northshore Middle School
Game

This game has two mechanics that use time, first there are wormholes that teleport you to another universe after you go in them, 
and then you have the black holes which make you trapped in time forever and 
spikes that kill you. The point of the game is to keep going through the 
wormholes and you will eventually end up in your own universe.
Languages and liberties used

I only used GDscript for the whole game, no additional libraries were used, 
python was used for prototyping and GitHub was used for source control.
Development process
I first made tiles and collisions for the player, 
and used the basic movement script to introduce gravity and movement to the game. I then added coins, spikes, and a 

splash screen making the code longer. 
I playtested the player version multiple times over the two weeks I was working on this project. 
Agent For the agent, I used GDscript and no other liberties, the agent basically 
is the same as the player, it has the same goals, same physics and same runtime, however the agent runs automatically.
Agent development process
For the agent, 
I first started by making a python game that calculates the best path from the start to the goal, and tries to avoid spikes. I used a 2d view 
of the world and a q-table, states, and actions. 
"

